  "page": {
    "language": "en",
    "title": "What KEE prevents us from losing — KnoEdg.NYC",
    "description": "Four New York City cases showing why disagreement, scope, provenance, and time must remain distinct in governed knowledge.",
    "canonical": "https://knoedg.nyc/kee-nyc-case-study/",
    "alternate": {
      "mediaType": "application/ld+json",
      "href": "https://knoedg.nyc/kee-nyc-case-study/index.jsonld",
      "title": "KEE NYC case study structured data"
    },
    "stylesheet": "/assets/styles.css",
    "contentBlocks": [
      {
        "type": "section",
        "id": "kee-nyc-case-study",
        "heading": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What KEE prevents us from losing"
          }
        ],
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Four New York City examples show what can be lost when a knowledge system collapses disagreement, scope, provenance, or time into a single answer."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "These examples are framed against KEE v0.10.0, but the downstream NYC fixtures were created under KEE v0.7.2 plus ADR-0049. This publication does not claim that the downstream NYC corpus conforms to KEE v0.10.0."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "section",
            "id": "case-1",
            "heading": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A disagreement can be preserved without turning source prestige into truth"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "What can go wrong: A naive system can either discard one source or treat every cross-source difference as a contradiction."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "What the governed record preserves: The useful governance result is preservation of the disagreement and its provenance. The historical contradiction edge is itself a governed classification, not proof that the records are logically incompatible."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "strong",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "A source is not the same thing as correctness."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "ordered": false,
                "items": [
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Overture Maps recorded Brooklyn Botanic Garden with the website https://linktr.ee/brooklynbotanic and coordinates (40.6686244, -73.96442177). Source: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "href": "https://docs.overturemaps.org/",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "source"
                        }
                      ],
                      "newWindow": true,
                      "accessibleNewWindowText": "opens in a new tab"
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "OpenStreetMap way 157016745 recorded Brooklyn Botanic Garden with website https://www.bbg.org and centroid (40.6677056, -73.9646509). Source: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "href": "https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/157016745",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "source"
                        }
                      ],
                      "newWindow": true,
                      "accessibleNewWindowText": "opens in a new tab"
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The historical governed fixture classified the two assertion records as contradicting each other. Source: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "href": "https://knoedg.org/nyc-knowledge-pack/assertion-metadata-bbg-per-overture",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "source"
                        }
                      ],
                      "newWindow": true,
                      "accessibleNewWindowText": "opens in a new tab"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "section",
                "id": "case-1-limitations",
                "heading": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Limitations"
                  }
                ],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "list",
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "The Overture record cites publisher documentation rather than the exact retrieved feature."
                        }
                      ],
                      [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "The historical contradiction classification remains challengeable."
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "section",
            "id": "case-2",
            "heading": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "An apparent contradiction can expose a modeling problem"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "What can go wrong: A naive system can treat different field values as proof that one source is wrong without checking whether the values answer different scoped questions."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "What the governed record preserves: The same historical fixture explains that a public-facing entrance address and a tax-lot address can both plausibly be legitimate for one building. This is a mixed result: the preserved context lets us challenge the fixture's own contradiction classification instead of silently canonizing it."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "strong",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "A governed contradiction marker is still a claim that can itself be challenged."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "ordered": false,
                "items": [
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "NYC's Library facilities dataset gives Brooklyn Central Library the address 10 Grand Army Plaza and BBL 3011830002. Source: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "href": "https://data.cityofnewyork.us/resource/feuq-due4.json?system=BPL",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "source"
                        }
                      ],
                      "newWindow": true,
                      "accessibleNewWindowText": "opens in a new tab"
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "PLUTO for BBL 3011830002 gives address 415 Flatbush Avenue and owner BROOKLYN PUBLIC LIBRARY. Source: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "href": "https://data.cityofnewyork.us/resource/64uk-42ks.json?bbl=3011830002",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "source"
                        }
                      ],
                      "newWindow": true,
                      "accessibleNewWindowText": "opens in a new tab"
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The historical governed fixture marks the facilities and PLUTO assertion records with a contradiction relation. Source: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "href": "https://knoedg.org/nyc-knowledge-pack/assertion-metadata-bpl-central-per-pluto",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "source"
                        }
                      ],
                      "newWindow": true,
                      "accessibleNewWindowText": "opens in a new tab"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "section",
                "id": "case-2-limitations",
                "heading": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Limitations"
                  }
                ],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "list",
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "This is intentionally not presented as a clean KEE success story."
                        }
                      ],
                      [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "The case study does not silently rewrite the historical downstream fixture."
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "section",
            "id": "case-3",
            "heading": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "More representations do not necessarily mean more independent evidence"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "What can go wrong: A naive system can count every representation as a separate vote and overstate evidential support."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "What the governed record preserves: Representation count and independent-provenance count answer different questions. Derived products can add value without becoming independent corroboration."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "strong",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "More records do not necessarily mean more independent evidence."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "ordered": false,
                "items": [
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The governed NYC Boundaries public view counts 46 active boundary representations across six publisher families. Source: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "href": "https://knoedg.nyc/nyc-boundaries/",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "source"
                        }
                      ],
                      "newWindow": true,
                      "accessibleNewWindowText": "opens in a new tab"
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Only DCP and the Census Gazetteer are included in that artifact's independent land-area comparison. Source: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "href": "https://knoedg.nyc/nyc-boundaries/",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "source"
                        }
                      ],
                      "newWindow": true,
                      "accessibleNewWindowText": "opens in a new tab"
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "geoBoundaries and Who's On First remain in the Census provenance cluster, while Overture representations remain in the OpenStreetMap provenance cluster for the relevant source lineage. Source: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "href": "https://knoedg.nyc/nyc-boundaries/",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "source"
                        }
                      ],
                      "newWindow": true,
                      "accessibleNewWindowText": "opens in a new tab"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "section",
                "id": "case-3-limitations",
                "heading": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Limitations"
                  }
                ],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "list",
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Independence is purpose-specific; a derived product may still add useful identifiers, hierarchy, packaging, or accessibility."
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "section",
            "id": "case-4",
            "heading": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A newer observation can replace an older one without erasing history"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "What can go wrong: A naive system can overwrite old observations or compare changed measurement vocabularies as if they meant exactly the same thing."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "What the governed record preserves: Currentness, historical validity, assertion time, capture time, and supersession are different dimensions. The three censuses also use different condition/status vocabularies, so raw totals must not be silently treated as directly comparable living-tree counts."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "strong",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Time is part of the knowledge."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "ordered": false,
                "items": [
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The 1995 NYC Street Tree Census fixture records 516,989 street-tree records and is governed as superseded by the 2005 record. Source: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "href": "https://data.cityofnewyork.us/resource/kyad-zm4j.json",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "source"
                        }
                      ],
                      "newWindow": true,
                      "accessibleNewWindowText": "opens in a new tab"
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The 2005 fixture records 592,372 street-tree records and is governed as superseded by the 2015 record. Source: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "href": "https://data.cityofnewyork.us/resource/29bw-z7pj.json",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "source"
                        }
                      ],
                      "newWindow": true,
                      "accessibleNewWindowText": "opens in a new tab"
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The 2015 fixture records 683,788 street-tree records, including 652,173 with status Alive, and is governed as the active record in this chain. Source: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "href": "https://data.cityofnewyork.us/resource/uvpi-gqnh.json",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "source"
                        }
                      ],
                      "newWindow": true,
                      "accessibleNewWindowText": "opens in a new tab"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "section",
                "id": "case-4-limitations",
                "heading": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Limitations"
                  }
                ],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "list",
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "The raw census totals are not presented as directly comparable living-tree counts."
                        }
                      ],
                      [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "The 2005 governed source records a disclosed upstream borough-name data-quality defect."
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "section",
            "id": "rights",
            "heading": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Rights and attribution"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "This page republishes factual summaries and public source references, not source geometry, media, or captured source bytes."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "ordered": false,
                "items": [
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "OpenStreetMap-origin material retains attribution to © OpenStreetMap contributors and the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0 reference."
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Overture Maps material retains attribution to Overture Maps Foundation and underlying OpenStreetMap contributors."
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "NYC Open Data facts retain exact source links; source datasets or source bytes require a fresh terms review before redistribution."
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "section",
            "id": "governance",
            "heading": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Governance and limitations"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "list",
                "ordered": false,
                "items": [
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The Brooklyn Central Library case is intentionally a mixed result: the historical fixture records a contradiction edge even though its own analysis says both addresses can plausibly be legitimate."
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The Brooklyn Botanic Garden contradiction edge is a governed historical classification, not proof of logical incompatibility."
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "More representations are not automatically more independent evidence."
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Time roles remain separate: represented assertion time, capture time, lifecycle state, and supersession are not collapsed."
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
